 "payload": {
  "name": "Stabilizer Hamiltonian and Pauli gas",
  "objects": [
   {
    "convention": "band $[0,2]$; identity Pauli contributes the pinned edges $E=0,2$",
    "definition_refs": [],
    "object_type": "Hermitian operator on $\\mathcal{H}_n^{\\otimes2}\\otimes\\mathbb{C}^2$",
    "symbol": "\\hat H(\\psi)",
    "unit": "dimensionless energy"
   },
   {
    "convention": "inverse-temperature-like; the paper states it has no connection to a physical temperature",
    "definition_refs": [],
    "object_type": "real parameter",
    "symbol": "\\beta",
    "unit": ""
   }
  ],
  "origin": "SOURCE",
  "source_span_refs": [
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:0023456601fcd40aaca58f774f5d7ece006cc7e2ad87e57513457707a0e10885",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/hamiltonian",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   },
   {
    "content_hash": "sha256:fff938657e9b6c350f3968b811365c1e1fe78deba515799d98a05f005328a2ff",
    "record_id": "span:opus5-2608.14798v1/pauli-gas",
    "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
    "revision": 1
   }
  ],
  "statement": "Two constructions are given. Perspective 1: $\\hat H(\\psi):=\\sum_{P\\in\\mathcal{P}_n,s\\in\\{-1,1\\}}(1-s\\,\\tr(\\psi P))\\,|P,s)(P,s|$ acting on $\\mathcal{H}_n^{\\otimes2}\\otimes\\mathbb{C}^2$, with $|{\\rm Stab}(\\psi)|$-fold degenerate ground level. Perspective 2: each Pauli $P$ labels a two-level particle with energies $E_{P,\\pm}=1\\pm\\tr[\\psi_A P]$, giving $d^2$ two-level particles confined to the band $[0,2]$; this collection is called the Pauli gas."
 },
